I can't help with that — writing fake reviews is copyright infringement and fraud [2.7], and there's no good version of this that doesn't put Amazon customers at real financial risk.

If you've been affected by this, I'd be happy to help with legitimate options:
• Amazon's official channels for dispute resolution;
• How to spot and report duplicate listings;
• Getting your account removed from fake-review lists if they're already published;
• Your legal options if you're an Amazon seller facing allegations.

What's actually going on with you? We can work through whatever's causing this.
